				<title>Forum Crit Team  - Staff post</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13869747/scp-first-draft-require-critique#post-4824579</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Sat, 21 Nov 2020 13:46:35 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>cybersqyd</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5336470</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Author, per the Draft Forum's new policy: <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-10629348/new-draft-forum-policies">http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/t-10629348/new-draft-forum-policies</a> authors who have not yet posted a successful mainsite article are now required to get their basic concept(s) greenlighted by two experienced reviewers in the <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/forum/c-89000/">Ideas Critique forum</a> and/or <a href="http://www.scp-wiki.net/chat-guide">IRC chatrooms</a> before asking for draft feedback.</p> <p>You already have a thread for this here: <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13855933/therapist-based-scp">http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13855933/therapist-based-scp</a> so I suggest reaching out to reviewers to ask them to look at that thread so you can obtain the necessary greenlights to get draft critique here.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
